predef: "l2src/tests/repro_zeroarg_ptr_cross_unit.h.lm1"

# Repro for lingvamyxa-ba (d6), 2026-09-15: a zero-argument function
# declared via `prototype:` (a cross-unit call, e.g. calling another
# already-ported unit's own p0_stream_event_new() from a different
# .lm2 file) fails to translate -- "unsupported body, frame=<name>".
# Found while porting l1src/parser.lm1:2634's `block_event: lm_p0_
# stream_event_new()` inside lm_p0_parse_fields_until_with_layout
# (parser-l2 Stage e Slice 5): p0_stream_event_new (Stage d's l2src/
# parser_stack_stream_port.lm2, already ported and already called the
# identical way IN-UNIT there, l2src/parser_stack_stream_port.lm2:
# 682) fails the moment the same call is made from a DIFFERENT unit
# (Stage e's own l2src/parser_field_parse_port.lm2) via a
# `prototype:` entry.
#
# CORRECTION (2026-09-15, follow-up): the line below originally read
# "fails to translate when its return type is a pointer... but the
# identical shape with an int return type translates fine" -- that
# claim was wrong, from a flawed control (the int-returning callee's
# real body was accidentally also present in the SAME file as its
# caller, so it resolved in-unit despite the prototype: entry,
# without ever exercising the cross-unit path this repro is about).
# A follow-up set of four properly cross-unit-only probes (d6's
# ticket, same day) measured the true trigger: zero FORMALS on a
# cross-unit prototype: call, regardless of return type -- int,
# LmP0StreamEvent* (this file's own shape) and char* all fail the
# same way; one formal with a pointer return already passes. This
# repro stays valid as a reproducing case (a zero-formal, pointer-
# return instance of the bug); only the characterization above it
# was too narrow. Every other cross-unit prototype call already in
# this port takes at least one argument (p0_new_node, p0_position_in_
# slice, p0_is_field_space, etc.), so zero formals specifically had
# never been exercised before either probe set. This file's own
# probe_zeroarg_ptr_source (fails) and probe_zeroarg_int_source (also
# fails, per the correction -- the comment below is left as written
# at commit time to show what was actually measured then) stand in
# for the real cross-unit source/caller split with a single header.

fn: probe_zeroarg_ptr_caller () int
    @: LmP0StreamEvent ev
    ev: probe_zeroarg_ptr_source()
    return: 0
end: probe_zeroarg_ptr_caller

fn: probe_zeroarg_int_caller () int
    int: v
    v: probe_zeroarg_int_source()
    return: v
end: probe_zeroarg_int_caller

fn: main () int
    return: 0
end: main
